---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';const roles=[['Parents','parents','Connect learning to everyday life. Help participants plan, practice household responsibilities, and reflect on growth.'],['Pastors & Teachers','pastors','Provide biblical instruction, answer questions, and help participants connect understanding with faithful living.'],['Mentors','mentors','Walk alongside a participant over time. Listen, model good habits, offer feedback, and encourage responsibility.'],['Skilled Church Members','skilled','Share practical experience. A mechanic, nurse, carpenter, homemaker, accountant, gardener, musician, or IT professional can help someone learn and demonstrate a useful skill.']];
---
<Layout title="For the Church"><section class="page-intro"><span class="eyebrow">Generations growing together</span><h1>A framework for personal investment.</h1><p class="lead">The church is full of people with wisdom to share.</p><p>Foundation Framework connects participants with parents, teachers, mentors, and skilled members of their own congregation. It creates opportunities for personal discipleship and practical apprenticeship.</p></section><section class="role-grid">{roles.map(([title,icon,text])=><article><Icon name={icon} size={36}/><h2>{title}</h2><p>{text}</p></article>)}</section><section class="two-column"><div><h2>Arrange involvement early</h2><p>Each challenge names the kind of help needed. Agree on the scope, supervision, and final demonstration before beginning. Involve parents or guardians when appropriate and follow your church’s established safeguarding practices.</p></div><div><h2>Make sign-off meaningful</h2><p>Review the requirements, observe the demonstration, and give specific feedback. Ask the participant to explain what they learned and how it could serve someone else. Your church determines authorized observers and keeps its own completion records.</p><p>The prototype stores participant readiness on one device. It cannot verify identities or record an adult’s approval.</p></div></section></Layout>
